{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>It is accounted as land of Refaim, etc.</b> Rashi explained, and this is his language: but this is not the one that I gave to Abraham. And I do not see the necessity for his words, for where do we find that HaShem said that these Refaim are not included? Moreover, since HaShem did not specify to Abraham a species of Refaim but stated it absolutely — all Refaim are included. And I saw that he hung his explanation on what the verse says ״הַהוּא יִקָּרֵא אֶרֶץ רְפָאִים״ (Deuteronomy 3:13) — the expression ״הַהוּא״ alerted us that there is another land, which, although it is called Refaim, is not in truth Refaim. And so he disclosed his opinion at the end of the chapter Elu Treifot (Chullin 77a), and there is no necessity for this. For the word ״הַהוּא״ — who says it comes to exclude other Refaim? Perhaps it comes to exclude another region of Argov that is not called land of Refaim except for that one. And so the mind inclines when we say that the word ״הַהוּא״ comes for precision, after the verse said concerning the land of Ammon and Moav that Refaim dwelt in it and HaShem gave the Refaim to Abraham in a general manner. Moreover, the word ״הַהוּא יִקָּרֵא״ diminishes only the naming — that it is not called so today ״land of Refaim״ but rather the land of Sichon and Og, and not the land of Ammon and Moav. Also, even if this land is accounted among the cities of the Refaim that HaShem mentioned to Abraham, it would not have been called at that time land of Refaim, because HaShem gave it to the children of Lot on account of the reverberation of Abraham's affairs as stated in their words (Rashi on verse 5), and from Abraham's portion they gave to Lot." "<b>And according to</b> this it may be precisely determined why concerning the land of Sichon and Og it says ״יִקָּרֵא״ and concerning the land of the children of Lot it says <b>תֵּחָשֵׁב</b>: for the land of Sichon and Og still bears its name upon it because Og was in it, but the land of the children of Lot is not called land of Refaim, although it is accounted as land of Refaim, and within the category of Refaim that HaShem told Abraham it is included. And the main point that I consider in this is that whatever the verse says is to be called land of Refaim is included in the gift of Abraham. And according to the words of the baraita of the Sifrei (part 2, §299) that I brought in parashat Matot, that the land of Sichon and Og is not included in the land that HaShem cut with Abraham, it is precisely determined what the verse said ״הַהוּא יִקָּרֵא אֶרֶץ רְפָאִים״ in this manner: הַהוּא יִקָּרֵא and not יֵחָשֵׁב — meaning, that the people call it land of Refaim, but according to truth it is not accounted as Refaim, because what people call it — land of Refaim — does not enter into the category of the Refaim that HaShem gave. And see nearby (Deuteronomy 3:13) what I wrote on the verse ״הַהוּא יִקָּרֵא אֶרֶץ רְפָאִים״, and there I explained in another manner."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ה׳ throughout is resolved as HaShem per voice rules. ״תלה זייניה״ is an Aramaic idiom meaning 'hung his [explanation],' i.e., based his interpretation on."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:42.307010545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}